October 2026: version 0.7.0
        * Discrete-event engine for Petri nets and timed nets: firing on markings, weighted, inhibitor and reset arcs, a capacity on each place, an optional duration on arcs.
        * Conflicts can be solved by priority, edited on the transitions.
        * Colors of tokens on the arcs. The position of a node lives in a layout, not in the node.
        * A timed event graph is drawn compactly, instead of being a type of net. The nodes added by the canonical form sit between their neighbors.
        * Big nets load in linear time. The file formats are a library of their own: PNML and the GRML of GreatSPN, as Symmetri reads them, and SVG.
        * Exports escape the names and keep the weights, the kinds and the colors of the arcs. File > Export lists only the formats that can write the active net.
        * Analysis of any net, apart from the (max,+) algebra: a path to the deadlock, bounds, liveness, invariants, from the tokens before the simulation.
        * The (max,+) algebra is its own library. The Gantt chart says why a flowshop shows only its machines.
        * Runtime: callbacks and executors, a net run as the function of a transition, journals saved and restored after a crash, CSV and XES, no memory taken at each step. Examples for a desktop, for services and for boards, timed against Symmetri.
        * The C++ code of the GRAFCETs of a document is generated and checked against the engine. A transition may fire when its downstream step is already active.
        * The editor follows a running program. Tokens, capacity, weight, duration and colors are edited with the mouse. Animated tokens follow their arc, bent or not. A hidden place draws one disk and the number of tokens.
        * An imported net is fitted in its view, also once it is unfolded. The journal clears when another document is shown. A notification says why a simulation ended.
        * The raylib backend is gone: GLFW3 everywhere. The project builds as C++20, without warnings, with clang-format, clang-tidy and a sanitizer in the CI.
        * Documentation of the analysis, the exports, the code generation and the debugger, and a text for each example.

October 2026: version 0.6.0
        * Editor redesign: mouse gestures, drawing, menus, analysis window, screenshots of the Petri view.
        * Editor sleeps in the main loop when nothing animates; analysis results are cached.
        * GRAFCET: IEC 60848 engine with infix receptivities, drawn actions, start from initial input values.
        * GRAFCET editor: control panel, timing diagram, simulation speed, captions scaled with zoom.
        * GEMMA example rewritten as a dryer.
        * Timed event graphs: tokens and durations displayed apart, critical circuit menu.
        * Flowshop: public API and Gantt chart.
        * Embeddable net viewer and TimedPetriNet.mk to build the library inside another project.
        * Max-plus symbols drawn with a merged math font.
        * Fixes: arc picking/deletion, dummy arc segfault, critical circuit crash after opening another net,
          Center View command, grid staying red.
        * Documentation rewritten as numbered chapters for beginners (editor, GRAFCET syntax and engine).

May 2026: version 0.5.0
        * Major editor refresh: menus, multi-graph documents, magnetic grid, force directed graph.
        * GRAFCET: adding (WIP) actions, forcage, display, multi GRAFCET (GEMMA).
        * Flowshop: import from flowshop description files, fix display of critical cycles.
        * Save format revision 4
        * Many major improvements and bug fixes in algorithms: Howard, critical cycles, sparse matrices
        * MQTT support replaced by ZeroMQ (WIP)
        * API: reset()/clear() split; merged run() and startUp()
        * Julia bindings extended
        * Dual licensing: GPL v3 or commercial.

Jan 2023: version 0.4.0
        * No longer use SFML, GUI is 100% DearIMGui
        * Without SFML can now compile with Emscripten for online version
        * Major code refacto (may regresions still present)
        * Update JSON format, fixing bug

May 2023: version 0.3.0
        * More export formats

March 2022: version 0.2.0
        * Use MyMakefile
        * Fixing compilation warnings
        * Adding unit tests

August 2021: version 0.1.0
        * Adding API for Julia
        * Minimal valid product
